}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form through $\\left(2,\\frac{5}{2}\\right)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)&=4(x-(2)), \\\\y&=4 x - \\frac{11}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=4x+\\left(- \\frac{11}{2}\\right), \\\\x&=\\frac{11}{8}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe intersection is $\\left(\\frac{11}{8},0\\right)$." 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761057 1075 #edb/ref 17592186761069 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761057 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761057 1077 "field-1" 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761057 1078 #edb/ref 17592186761069 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761057 1079 #uuid "105f3b7c-32d3-5721-896a-80a7e4481dd8" 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761058 1080 "0" 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761058 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761058 1083 #uuid "1bc39092-d8e9-5453-8c18-574cb938a383" 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761059 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761066 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761059 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761067 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761059 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761059 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=3\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}}-3$ at the point $(8,9)$ intersects the $y$-axis.\n\nThe intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values." 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761059 1072 #uuid "29406d9f-bf1b-52ad-b004-ccc298593364" 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761059 1074 "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=3 x^{\\frac{2}{3}} - 3, \\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{2}{x^{\\frac{1}{3}}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{x}}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_t=f'(8)&=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt[3]{(8)}}=1, \\\\m_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\\frac{1}{(1)}=-1.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form through $(8,9)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-(9)&=-1(x-(8)), \\\\y&=- x + 17.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $y$-axis, $x=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny&=-1\\cdot 0+(17), \\\\y&=17.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe intersection is $(0,17)$." 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761060 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761057 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761060 1068 #edb/ref 17592186761076 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761060 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761060 1071 "Find where the normal line to the curve $y=\\sqrt{x^{3}}-1$ at the point $(4,7)$ intersects the $x$-axis.\n\nThe intersection is $(${{field-1}}$,$ {{field-2}}$)$. Give exact values." 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761060 1072 #uuid "2ed6c176-c8ce-5e49-a7ef-0346fa82cc02" 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761060 1074 "Rewrite the radical or reciprocal using powers, then differentiate.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x)&=x^{\\frac{3}{2}} - 1, \\\\f'(x)&=\\frac{3 x^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{2}=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{x}}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope and take its negative reciprocal to find the normal slope.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nm_t=f'(4)&=\\frac{3 \\sqrt{(4)}}{2}=3, \\\\m_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}&=-\\frac{1}{(3)}=- \\frac{1}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse point-slope form through $(4,7)$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-(7)&=- \\frac{1}{3}(x-(4)), \\\\y&=- \\frac{x}{3} + \\frac{25}{3}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-axis, $y=0$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n0&=- \\frac{1}{3}x+\\left(\\frac{25}{3}\\right), \\\\x&=25.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe intersection is $(25,0)$." 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761061 1075 #edb/ref 17592186761063 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761061 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 13194139547578 17592186576411 true] [17592186761061 1077 "field-1" 1319413